[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "2605090000-adr-2605082000-phase-a-status", :doc/title "ADR-2605082000 Phase A — Status Snapshot 2026-05-09", :doc/status "active", :doc/doc_type "reference", :doc/source-format "edn", :doc/body "\n# ADR-2605082000 Phase A — Status Snapshot\n\nCaptured 2026-05-09 after 44 iterations of transform work. This doc is\n**non-authoritative** (running progress note); ADR-2605082000 / 2100 / 2200\nremain the SSoT for design intent.\n\n## Live Metrics\n\nRun `node 70-tools/scripts/lint/audit-langgraph-self-evolution-debt.mjs`\nto refresh. Current snapshot:\n\n| Metric | Value | ADR target |\n|---|---|---|\n| assistant data-share (live) | **82.8%** (53 / 64) | 100% |\n| node      data-share (live) | **53.3%** (73 / 137) | 100% |\n| live mcp_tool nodes | 73 | (grows) |\n| live py_primitive (code-island) | 64 | 0 |\n| live py_factory (code-island) | 11 | 0 |\n| dispatcher handlers | 103 (17 actors + 3 generic primitives) | — |\n\nThe audit script does two key corrections:\n\n1. **same-PK upsert detection** (iter 41): when the same `assistant_id`\n   is INSERTed twice with different `kind`, the later wins (RW upsert\n   semantics). Without this, builtin py_factory rows that bulk-51\n   overwrites with topology rows would be double-counted.\n2. **`.down.sql` exclusion** (iter 42): rollback files contain\n   restoration INSERTs that don't reflect live state.\n\n## Phase A Migrations (14 deployed-ready, plus 4 pin-flips ready)\n\nListed in apply order:\n\n| # | Migration | scope (live mcp_tool nodes added) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | r_20260509170000_topology_saikin_cycle_v2_mcp | saikin (5) |\n| 2 | r_20260509200000_topology_ki_cycle_v2_mcp | ki (5, with const.echo for skip_bloom) |\n| 3 | r_20260509230000_adsk_ingest_dataset_v2_mcp | adsk (1) |\n| 4 | r_20260509240000_aria_canonical_v2_mcp | aria (7 assistants × 1 node = 7) |\n| 5 | r_20260509250000_isbn_canonical_v2_mcp | isbn (6) |\n| 6 | r_20260509260000_agentEconomy_canonical_v2_mcp | agentEconomy (1 node + 8 shelf) |\n| 7 | r_20260509270000_onion_osMessaging_canonical_v2_mcp | onion + osMessaging (4) |\n| 8 | r_20260509280000_publicMalakAds_patent_canonical_v2_mcp | publicMalakAds + patent (4) |\n| 9 | r_20260509290000_coverageGap_yoro_canonical_v2_mcp | coverageGap + yoro_platform_pulse (6) |\n| 10 | r_20260509300000_wellbecoming_canonical_v2_mcp | wellbecoming (10, 9 assistants) |\n| 11 | r_20260509320000_shosha_canonical_v2_mcp | shosha (15, 6/7 assistants) |\n| 12 | r_20260509330000_shinshi_canonical_v2_mcp | shinshi (3, conditional preserved) |\n| 13 | r_20260509350000_shinka_canonical_v2_mcp | shinka (1) |\n| 14 | r_20260509360000_koke_canonical_v2_mcp | koke (5) |\n\nPin-flip migrations (operator-gated):\n- r_20260509180000_flip_saikin_cycle_v2_pin\n- r_20260509220000_flip_ki_cycle_v2_pin\n\n## Generic Primitives (3)\n\n| NSID | Replaces | Live consumers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `com.etzhayyim.tools.const.echo` | identity / no-op nodes | ki.cycle.v2 skip_bloom |\n| `com.etzhayyim.tools.audit.emit` | per-actor `emit_audit` py_primitive | shosha v2 ×5, shinshi v2 ×1 |\n| `com.etzhayyim.tools.llm.chat` | pure-LLM py_primitive | (shelf-stocked, animeka future) |\n\nAdding a 4th generic primitive (e.g. `tools.sql.query`) is the way to\ndata-resolve the remaining `sa_query`-style nodes without per-actor\nrefactor; constraints under design.\n\n## Dispatcher Architecture\n\n`kotodama/mcp_dispatch.py`:\n\n- `_DEFAULT_ACTORS` is a list of dicts. Three resolution patterns:\n  - **default convention**: `kotodama.<actor>_worker_main:task_<snake>`\n  - **fn_template override**: per-actor `module` + `fn_template` for\n    primitives that live elsewhere (e.g. aria_signal, shosha, isbn)\n  - **explicit mapping**: per-method dict for heterogeneous actors\n    (e.g. wellbecoming spans 4 sub-modules)\n- 3 override builders: `_build_const_overrides` / `_build_audit_overrides`\n  / `_build_llm_overrides` register `com.etzhayyim.tools.*` namespace tools.\n- Tool functions are imported lazily; missing modules WARN-and-skip\n  (boot stays robust).\n\nResolver path (langgraph_node_resolvers):\n\n```\nmcp://<nsid>\n  → SELECT actor_host FROM vertex_mcp_tool_def WHERE nsid=$1 AND enabled=true\n    (60s in-process cache)\n  → POST https://{actor_host}/xrpc/com.etzhayyim.mcp.message\n    body = {\"method\":\"tools/call\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"<nsid>\",\"arguments\":{...}}}\n  → Worker proxies to dispatcher /xrpc/com.etzhayyim.mcp.message\n  → mcp_dispatch.handle_envelope → MCP_HANDLERS[nsid] → task_*\n  → result wrapped in {\"result\": ...}\n  → returned to LangGraph node → state[result_key]\n```\n\nEnd-to-end smoke test (no DB / no HTTP): `tests/test_mcp_e2e_smoke.py`.\n\n## Tooling\n\n| Tool | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `70-tools/scripts/lint/lint-langgraph-py-primitive-ban.mjs` | reject new `kind='py_primitive'` rows |\n| `70-tools/scripts/lint/audit-langgraph-bulk51-classify.mjs` | classify py_primitive nodes by kind candidate |\n| `70-tools/scripts/lint/audit-langgraph-self-evolution-debt.mjs` | live data-share / code-island metric |\n| `70-tools/scripts/codegen/gen-bulk51-mcp-migration-draft.mjs` | per-actor migration drafts (lexicon + SQL stubs) |\n| `.github/workflows/langgraph-py-primitive-ban-lint.yml` | CI gate on new py_primitive |\n| `.github/workflows/langgraph-debt-trend.yml` | CI debt metric on every PR |\n\n## Phase A Remaining (operator-gated)\n\n| Item | Status |\n|---|---|\n| saikin pin flip | r_20260509180000 ready |\n| ki pin flip | r_20260509220000 ready |\n| adsk Worker scaffold | needs creation OR actor_host UPDATE |\n| aria / isbn / shosha / etc Worker scaffolds | needs creation per actor |\n| Lexicon authoring (currently stubbed `'{\"type\":\"object\"}'`) | follow-up batch |\n\n## Phase B / C Out of Scope\n\nThe remaining 64 live py_primitive nodes are confirmed self_logic in\n12 actors (lawfirm / kaisya / etzhayyim / warehouse / copyright_* /\necho / tsukuru / yoro_product_ingest / animeka mixed nodes /\nshosha_agent_loop). Migration requires:\n\n1. **Phase B**: extracting their work into `kotodama/primitives/<actor>.py`\n   modules with `task_*` functions. Per-actor refactor (~1-3 days each).\n2. **Phase C**: replacing inline SQL nodes with `kind=sql_udf` after\n   designing the matching Kotoba/Datomic UDFs (23 candidate nodes per audit).\n\nThese are outside ADR-2605082000's data-only-INSERT goal and require\nreal Python refactoring — tracked under\n`deps.toml [[migrations]] langgraph-bulk-51-py-primitive-migration`\nPhase B/C.\n\n## How to extend (new actor)\n\nFor an actor whose `task_*` functions already exist:\n\n1. Add a dict entry to `_DEFAULT_ACTORS` (`actor`, `methods`, optional\n   `module` + `fn_template`, or `mapping`).\n2. Add a regression test (one of the existing per-actor tests as template).\n3. Author SQL migration: vertex_mcp_tool_def seed + assistant.v2 +\n   mcp_tool nodes + supersedes UPDATE.\n4. (Eventually) author proper lexicons under\n   `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/<actor>/`.\n5. (Eventually) deploy `<actor>.etzhayyim.com` Worker matching saikin/ki template.\n\nThe dispatcher will auto-wire after step 1; the data layer responds\nafter step 3 is applied.\n", :doc/path "90-docs/2605090000-adr-2605082000-phase-a-status.edn", :doc/source-repo "root", :doc/topic "langgraph-graph-definition-as-data", :doc/last_verified "2026-05-09", :doc/date "2026-05-09", :doc/authoritative false, :doc/related ["adr-2605082000-langgraph-graph-definition-as-data" "adr-2605082100-langgraph-checkpointer-storage" "adr-2605082200-pyzeebe-handler-thin-dispatcher-contract" "adr-2605080000-distributed-cognitive-actor-system"]}]
